Sectoare de activitate: Tehnologia informației și servicii informatice
Medialine România is part of the Medialine Group , an IT solutions provider founded in 1999 with operations in Germany, Austria and Romania. We deliver IT infrastructure, private cloud, managed services, cybersecurity and business solutions to mid-sized and enterprise clients across multiple industries. Our Bucharest team runs and secures the infrastructure of both Medialine and our managed services clients, working in an international group environment. The team is expanding, and we are looking for a skilled System Administrator – Windows & Linux Server to join our dynamic and innovative environment.
 POSITION DESCRIPTION 
 Department: IT&C and Managed Services | Reports to: Manager IT&C and Managed Services | Location: Bucharest | Employment type: full-time, permanent
 About the role 
 We are looking for a System Administrator to ensure the stable, secure and high-performing operation of the Windows and Linux server infrastructure (physical and virtual) for Medialine and for our managed services clients. The role involves direct responsibility for the availability, security and documentation of the managed environments, in close collaboration with the IT&C team.
 Responsibilities 
Installation, configuration and maintenance of Windows and Linux servers (physical and virtual), together with the related services;
Troubleshooting and performance optimisation of Windows and Linux servers;
Ensuring server security: access control, firewall configuration, malware prevention, periodic application of updates and patches;
Administration of Active Directory services (AD, DNS, GPO);
Monitoring server health and performance and proactive intervention on alerts;
Ensuring reliable backup and recovery processes, including periodic restore testing;
Keeping IT documentation up to date (configurations, procedures, infrastructure diagrams);
Managing incidents and requests through the ticketing system, in compliance with the agreed SLAs.
 Must have 
Solid experience in administering Microsoft Windows Server 2016/2019/2022/2025 and the associated services: DHCP, DNS, Active Directory, WSUS etc.;
Working experience with Fortinet security equipment (FortiGate firewalls), including the configuration and administration of security policies, VPN (IPsec/SSL), interfaces and routing, as well as network traffic monitoring;
Experience in server-level networking (TCP/IP, VLAN, basic routing, firewall);
Linux Server administration knowledge (one enterprise distribution: RHEL/CentOS, Ubuntu Server, Debian or SUSE);
English at a professional level (written and spoken).
 Nice to have 
Experience with ticketing solutions (Jira or similar);
Experience with virtualisation environments (VMware vSphere, Hyper-V, Proxmox);
Experience in managed services environments / support for multiple clients.
 Candidate profile 
Team spirit and result orientation – a "get it done" mindset;
Analytical capacity and strong problem-solving skills;
Responsible, organised way of working, rigorous in documentation;
Availability for occasional interventions outside working hours, according to the team's planning;
Real commitment to teamwork and to the quality of the services delivered.
 Education and certifications 
Completed higher education or full professional qualification in an IT / technical field;
Certifications in systems and network administration (MCSE / Microsoft Certified: Windows Server, CCNA, LPIC, RHCSA or similar) are an advantage.
 What we offer 
 A motivating and dynamic work environment with an experienced and supportive team 
Professional environment, access to leading-edge technologies
Professional development programs – certifications
Possibility to travel abroad
Employee events
Employee mobile phone
Medical insurance
Private pension
 Why Medialine 
 We are a company where the people who run the infrastructure know the clients, own the results and see the impact of their work. Growth here comes from what you deliver, not from your position in an org chart.
 It is an extraordinary time to be in business. As digital transformation continues to accelerate, Medialine is at the center of this change, supporting our clients' digital journeys and offering our professionals exciting career opportunities.
 At Medialine, our success comes from the talent and commitment of our professionals. As one team, we share the challenges and rewards that come from growing our company, which reinforces our culture of ownership. All our professionals benefit from the value we collectively create.
 Be part of building one of the largest independent technology and business services firms in the world.
 Build your career with us! Apply now or contact us at info@medialine.ro .
